WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:04.421
We would like to share some
information about our network.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:11.845
When we start season two we see
the aftermath, the chaos.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:16.016
There was such a cost to that
moment of complete honesty.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.018
Alex!
-Just keep your phone on,

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.186
I'll call you.

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:23.065
In this season our characters
are searching for who they are

00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:24.983
and trying to get through it in
a world

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.735
that's transitioning
very quickly.

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:28.946
The Morning Show is in a place
of real flux,

00:00:28.946 --> 00:00:30.447
I mean Alex Levy
has left the show

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:32.491
and of course
the fallout from Mitch Kessler

00:00:32.491 --> 00:00:34.493
having left the show
is still resonating.

00:00:34.618 --> 00:00:36.578
UBA is a changed environment.

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.957
It's noticeably more diverse,
young, there are more women.

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:43.043
We are no longer running the
show from the perspective 

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:46.088
of the white male patriarchy,
we have moved on.

00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:47.839
Everything's different
this season.

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:49.925
(shouts)

00:00:49.925 --> 00:00:53.804
In season two we meet Alex in a
very serene place. 

00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:55.514
I think she had to
get out of the chaos.

00:00:55.514 --> 00:00:58.809
Please come back. You've
become a powerful voice

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:01.561
in the rebuilding and the
rebranding of a toxic empire

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.980
that… it's gonna rise.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:05.816
There's a tremendous amount of
guilt that she's feeling,

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:07.776
her hypocrisy within herself.

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:10.612
She sort of became a feminist
hero and I think she has this

00:01:10.612 --> 00:01:12.072
secret guilt that she isn't. 

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:14.950
She has this history with Mitch
that she's ashamed of.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.869
But something about her still
needs to feel relevant

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:20.664
and there's obviously still more
for her to excavate.

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:22.124
You know thing are gonna have to
be different

00:01:22.124 --> 00:01:25.043
if we're gonna resume this,
quote-unquote, partnership.

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:30.048
I was the one exposing the 
and I decided to include you.

00:01:29.256 --> 00:01:31.842
Bradley steps into a
position where

00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:33.844
she's trying to play the game,

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:34.428
she's trying to get ahead.

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:37.556
Bradley becomes the
number one lead anchor.

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.558
Whenever people think about
The Morning Show, 

00:01:39.558 --> 00:01:40.642
I want them to think of me.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:42.894
And she thinks she's in control.

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:46.898
Laura Peterson comes up to
mentor Bradley Jackson.

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:48.608
I don't think they're using you
in the right way.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.027
You're bigger than that.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:52.529
When Bradley meets her
it's just hero worship,

00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:54.531
there's just this
larger-than-life character.

00:01:54.865 --> 00:01:58.160
The energy between Reese's
character and my character is

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.538
really interesting to watch
because you really see Reese's

00:02:01.538 --> 00:02:04.958
character grow, just by
being in Laura's orbit.

00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.878
I'm making a toast.

00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:10.630
These two women, they changed
the course of human history

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.466
and we've got them.

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:16.803
The personal stake that Cory had
in season one was winning.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.431
He didn't seem concerned about
the consequences.

00:02:19.431 --> 00:02:21.475
You're a dead man. 
-Said the corpse. 

00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:23.769
All of the sudden you're
watching Pinocchio become

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:26.688
a real boy and he has to
manage real feelings.

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:31.485
This is a battle for the
soul of the universe.

00:02:31.485 --> 00:02:34.404
The show brings up so many
great talking points

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:37.032
about the world and
people being human.

00:02:37.032 --> 00:02:40.160
People relate to shows
where human beings

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.620
ask the deeper question.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.580
A show on a network allowed the

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.540
worst behavior to be
permissible.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.376
Does that line up
with your experience?

00:02:47.376 --> 00:02:49.252
I think some people are
ready to talk,

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:50.879
some people are not
ready for that.

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:53.382
It's okay to be anywhere you
want on that spectrum

00:02:53.382 --> 00:02:54.424
but that's going to be tested.

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:56.593
There is a pattern of behavior

00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:59.304
around here that disadvantages
the people of color.

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:03.558
We all develop a different
relationship with America

00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:04.559
and I think that there are a lot

00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:07.938
of people who are really
re-evaluating their place.

00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:09.856
It's been brought to my
attention that for me

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.859
to use that term might be 
considered insensitive.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:17.364
So much of this show is showing
these real world relationships

00:03:17.364 --> 00:03:21.034
unfold in real time and it just
allows the audience to

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.829
organically go on this journey

00:03:23.829 --> 00:03:26.832
to answer some pretty
complicated questions.

00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:29.292
You mean something Alex, you do.

00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:32.879
As a leader, as a feminist, and
I want you to be these things.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:35.132
What you thought was going to
happen at the beginning

00:03:35.132 --> 00:03:37.676
of season two, all of a sudden
there's these detours

00:03:37.676 --> 00:03:39.636
that you didn't think about
along the way.

00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:41.471
We have more incredible
story lines,

00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:43.515
much bigger and much
more impactful

00:03:43.515 --> 00:03:45.058
than you could ever imagine

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.394
Camera two get the both of them,
two shot.

00:03:47.394 --> 00:03:49.229
Onward and upward.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:53.024
♪♪

